<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Mackie International H1 pretax profit down.</title>
<headline>Mackie International H1 pretax profit down.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>					  (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		9.8		    vs 13.7</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.7		    vs 3.7</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    1.04		   vs 1.32</p>
<p> Turnover		   9.47		   vs 10.92</p>
<p> Operating profit	 1.05		   vs 1.18</p>
<p> Interest payable	 0.12		   vs nil</p>
<p> Tax charge		 0.09		   vs nil</p>
<p> Net taxed		  0.95		   vs 1.32</p>
<p> Retained profit	  0.59		   vs 0.97</p>
<p> Record date		October 8</p>
<p> Pay date		   October 18</p>
<p> Ex-dividend date	 September 30</p>
<p>NOTE - Northern Ireland-based precision engineering company Mackie International Plc said a review of operations was under way to determine how to streamline the firm's resources to reduce vulnerability to difficult trading conditions.</p>
<p>&quot;The sales and profit performance has been achieved despite the difficult trading conditions encountered during the period,&quot; executive chairman Patrick Dougan said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;It is envisaged that the trading climate will remain difficult through to the year end, however the management strategy to broaden the busines base will lessen dependency on traditional markets,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom 353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
